  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find the column with the line of 5s\n    line_col = None\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 5:\n                line_col = c\n                break\n        if line_col is not None:\n            break\n    \n    if line_col is None:\n        return grid\n    \n    # Find all special pixels (non-zero, non-5)\n    specials = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val != 0 and val != 5:\n                specials.append((r, c, val))\n    \n    # Create output as copy\n    output = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    last_col = cols - 1\n    \n    for r, c, val in specials:\n        # Clear original position\n        output[r][c] = 0\n        \n        # Place at the end of the same row\n        output[r][last_col] = val\n        \n        # Calculate target column for row 0 placement\n        target_col = line_col + r\n        \n        if target_col <= last_col:\n            # Place at row 0, column (line_col + row)\n            output[0][target_col] = val\n        else:\n            # Find the nearest row at or above with a 5 in the line column\n            target_row = None\n            for rr in range(r, -1, -1):\n                if grid[rr][line_col] == 5:\n                    target_row = rr\n                    break\n            if target_row is not None:\n                output[target_row][last_col] = val\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find the column with the line of 5s\n    line_col = None\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 5:\n                line_col = c\n                break\n        if line_col is not None:\n            break\n    \n    if line_col is None:\n        return grid\n    \n    # Find all special pixels (non-zero, non-5)\n    specials = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val != 0 and val != 5:\n                specials.append((r, c, val))\n    \n    # Create output as copy\n    output = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    last_col = cols - 1\n    \n    for r, c, val in specials:\n        # Clear original position\n        output[r][c] = 0\n        \n        # Place at the end of the same row\n        output[r][last_col] = val\n        \n        # Calculate target column for row 0 placement\n        target_col = line_col + r\n        \n        if target_col <= last_col:\n            # Place at row 0, column (line_col + row)\n            output[0][target_col] = val\n        else:\n            # Find the nearest row at or above with a 5 in the line column\n            target_row = None\n            for rr in range(r, -1, -1):\n                if grid[rr][line_col] == 5:\n                    target_row = rr\n                    break\n            if target_row is not None:\n                output[target_row][last_col] = val\n    \n    return output",
